        {
          "title": "Sequence Containers: vector, deque, list",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. vector",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Contiguous== dynamic array: O(1) access, amortized O(1) `push_back`",
                "Insert/erase in the middle is **O(n)** (elements shift)",
                "Capacity grows geometrically, about ==1.5x to 2x==",
                "`reserve(n)`: preallocates capacity, `size()` unchanged",
                "`resize(n)`: changes size, new elements value-initialized"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. deque and list",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Access",
                "Ends",
                "Middle",
                "Memory"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "vector",
                  "O(1)",
                  "back O(1)",
                  "O(n)",
                  "contiguous"
                ],
                [
                  "deque",
                  "O(1)",
                  "both O(1)",
                  "O(n)",
                  "chunked blocks"
                ],
                [
                  "list",
                  "none",
                  "both O(1)",
                  "O(1) at iterator",
                  "linked nodes"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:deque}: `push_front` and `push_back` O(1), but not contiguous",
                "{purple:list}: doubly linked, no random access, no `operator[]`",
                "`splice` moves nodes between lists in ==O(1)=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "vector<int> v{3,1,2};",
                "v.push_back(4); v.emplace_back(5);",
                "cout << v.back() << '\\n';",
                "v.pop_back();",
                "v.erase(v.begin() + 1);",
                "cout << v.size() << '\\n';"
              ],
              "note": "v: {3,1,2,4,5} then {3,2,4}"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "5",
                "3"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistakes",
              "text": "`v[i]` is **unchecked**; `v.at(i)` throws `out_of_range`. `vector<bool>` is a ==packed bitset==, not a real container of bool."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
