    {
      "title": "priority_queue and Container Adaptors",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "priority_queue and Container Adaptors",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. priority_queue Basics",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Binary ==heap== adaptor over `vector`",
                "`top()` {green:O(1)}; `push` / `pop` {blue:O(log n)}",
                "==Max-heap== by default: largest on top",
                "Template args: {purple:type}, {purple:container}, {purple:comparator}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> pq;",
                "pq.push(5); pq.push(1); pq.push(3);",
                "cout << pq.top();"
              ],
              "note": "min-heap: greater<int> as 3rd argument"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "1"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Custom Order with a Lambda",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "auto cmp = [](const P& a, const P& b){",
                "    return a.d > b.d;",
                "};",
                "priority_queue<P, vector<P>, decltype(cmp)> pq(cmp);"
              ],
              "note": "pass cmp to the constructor too"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Inverted logic",
              "text": "==less== means **lower priority**, so `a.d > b.d` puts the smallest `d` on top."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. stack, queue and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`stack` and `queue` are adaptors over ==deque==",
                "Only `push`, `pop`, `top` (or `front`/`back`) exposed",
                "No iterators, no traversal",
                "`top()` / `pop()` on empty is ==undefined behavior==: check `empty()`",
                "`pop()` returns **void**: read `top()` first",
                "No in-place update: push a new one, skip stale entries"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
