            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "An ==iterator== is a pointer-like handle",
                "`begin()` is the first element; `end()` is ==one past the last==, never dereference it",
                "Categories: input, forward, bidirectional, ==random-access=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. What Invalidates",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Container",
                "Insert",
                "Erase"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`vector`",
                  "`push_back` may reallocate: {red:all} iterators, refs, pointers",
                  "Change point onward"
                ],
                [
                  "`deque`",
                  "Middle: all. Ends: iterators, ==not refs==",
                  "Middle: all"
                ],
                [
                  "`list` `map` `set`",
                  "{green:Never}",
                  "Erased one only"
                ],
                [
                  "`unordered_*`",
                  "Rehash: iterators",
                  "Erased one only"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Safe Erase",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "for (auto it = v.begin(); it != v.end();) {",
                "  if (pred(*it)) it = v.erase(it);",
                "  else ++it;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "erase returns the next valid iterator"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistakes",
              "text": "Erasing inside a range-for, or `erase(it++)` on a vector. Use erase-remove: `v.erase(remove(v.begin(), v.end(), x), v.end());`"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why not erase in a range-for?** It invalidates the hidden iterator",
                "**What does erase return?** The next valid iterator",
                "**Does list insert invalidate?** No, never"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
