              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Spot the bug: `for (auto it = v.begin(); it != v.end(); ++it) if (*it == 2) v.erase(it);`",
              "a_bullets": [
                "erase invalidates `it`, so the following ++it is undefined behavior",
                "Fix: `it = v.erase(it)` in the if branch, `++it` only in the else",
                "Or use the erase-remove idiom"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What does this print?",
              "example_code": [
                "map<string,int> m;",
                "if (m[\"a\"] == 0) {}",
                "cout << m.size();"
              ],
              "a_bullets": [
                "1",
                "operator[] inserts a default value 0 for a missing key",
                "Use find or count to look up without inserting"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What is wrong with `accumulate(v.begin(), v.end(), 0)` on a vector<long long> holding two 3000000000s?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The init 0 is an int, so the running sum is an int and overflows",
